# pyro_packedmipmap

- Label: Pyro Packed MipMap
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_packedmipmap.html
- Summary (EN): Builds an in-place mipmap of a VDB: several half-resolution copies of the same VDB packed so many levels fit in roughly the original storage. A technical node meant to be computed once and sampled by other nodes, not an end-user effect.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Packed MipMap construit un conteneur multi-résolution d'un VDB, réutilisable par les autres nœuds Pyro, et non un VDB exploitable directement.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: Float or Vector VDB to compute the mipmap for"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: sets which VDB types the node accepts (see the Signatures glossary entry on the page)", "MipMap Depth: number of resolution levels stored, each half the resolution of the previous; most nodes use the first three levels; maximum 10"]

- Caveats: ["The output is not a valid VDB and must not be used as one; it is a mipmap container with the input topology but values encoding several resolutions", "Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, works in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education"]

